> 
> Rserve is not working in my system.

Well, then how do you get to that error at all? It would fail much earlier if you didn't have Rserve running ...


> It seems there is a problem as I am using a Windows system.

You can use Rserve on Windows, it just won't support parallel connections.


> I altough have a small query do I need to use Rserve even if I use JRI for the R and Java Interaction?
> 

JRI and Rserve are entirely different ways to call R from Java. If you already use JRI then calling Rserve doesn't make much sense - the point of Rserve is that you avoid embedding the R process into your application (which is what JRI does).

But neither has anything to do with the original question you posted ...

Cheers,
Simon



